  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0131">Definition <span data-tag="0131">12.25.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $K^{\bullet , \bullet }$ be a double complex. We say the spectral sequence $({}'E_ r, {}'d_ r)_{r \geq 0}$ <em>weakly converges to $H^ n(\text{Tot}(K^{\bullet , \bullet }))$</em>, <em>abuts to $H^ n(\text{Tot}(K^{\bullet , \bullet }))$</em>, or <em>converges to $H^ n(\text{Tot}(K^{\bullet , \bullet }))$</em> if Definition <a href="/tag/012U" data-tag="012U">12.24.9</a> applies. Similarly we say the spectral sequence $({}''E_ r, {}''d_ r)_{r \geq 0}$ <em>weakly converges to $H^ n(\text{Tot}(K^{\bullet , \bullet }))$</em>, <em>abuts to $H^ n(\text{Tot}(K^{\bullet , \bullet }))$</em>, or <em>converges to $H^ n(\text{Tot}(K^{\bullet , \bullet }))$</em> if Definition <a href="/tag/012U" data-tag="012U">12.24.9</a> applies. </p>
